<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:h="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" version="1.0" name="Handoff" initial="idle"><metadata><h:section id="documentation"><h:h2>Handoff — actor contract</h:h2><h:p><h:strong>Actor invariant: </h:strong>Server-only invoked adapter, idempotency, audit and manual user approval.</h:p><h:p><h:strong>Specification: </h:strong>ACT-HANDOFF in <h:a href="../system.xml">system.xml</h:a>. These comments use XHTML namespace h: and are not executable SCXML actions.</h:p><h:h3>I/O contracts invoked by this actor</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-HANDOFF">review.handoff.submit</h:a> — HandoffRequest → HandoffResult | Fault; external-write, provider-dedupe-required, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-020, FL-022; requirements: REQ-049, REQ-050, REQ-051, REQ-065</h:li></h:ul></h:section></metadata><state id="idle">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-idle"><h:h3>State: idle</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>handoff.dispatch</h:code> → dispatching</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="handoff.dispatch" target="dispatching"/>
  </state>
  <state id="dispatching">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-dispatching"><h:h3>State: dispatching</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>handoff.success</h:code> → delivered<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-HANDOFF"> [typed result: IO-HANDOFF]</h:a></h:li><h:li><h:code>handoff.failed</h:code> → failed<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-HANDOFF"> [typed result: IO-HANDOFF]</h:a></h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="handoff.success" target="delivered"/>
    <transition event="handoff.failed" target="failed"/>
  </state>
  <state id="delivered"><metadata><h:section id="state-delivered"><h:h3>State: delivered</h:h3><h:p>No outgoing transitions in this version. This state is terminal until the host ends or restores the actor.</h:p></h:section></metadata></state>
  <state id="failed">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-failed"><h:h3>State: failed</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>handoff.dispatch</h:code> → dispatching</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="handoff.dispatch" target="dispatching"/>
  </state>
</scxml>
